{
  "id": "20_drone_refine",
  "title": "Entity Marking: Spraying a Front-Facing Accent",
  "label": "无人机检查与标记",
  "duration": 31.4,
  "voice_timing": [
    {
      "start": 0.2,
      "duration": 9.04,
      "text": "The drone appears instantly on the terrace, with four counter-rotating rotor arms clearly defined. The visual spinning animations work hand-in-hand with genuine dynamic physics forces.",
      "source": "modules/20_drone_refine/audio/0088895d0713e46b00fe.wav"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.489999999999998,
      "duration": 11.84,
      "text": "Because quadcopters are geometrically symmetrical, reading their heading during rapid aerial spins can be tricky. We whip out the Brush and paint a vivid front accent badge—a two-second touch that brings instant personality to the drone.",
      "source": "modules/20_drone_refine/audio/39b21e5f351e98aac271.wav"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.58,
      "duration": 9.44,
      "text": "Sturdy landing feet ensure clean clearance. While Modeling tools can easily add camera gimbals or cosmetic housings, genuine flight behavior always flows from the underlying physics components.",
      "source": "modules/20_drone_refine/audio/700dee662da4350f181c.wav"
    }
  ],
